{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/450105-question-for-st-s","id":450105,"title":"question for st's","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-19T21:31:14-07:00","id":450105,"title":"question for st's","content":"how do you entice your players to actually attempt to follow their pilgrimage and not just become heavy handed power houses that they can easily become<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5414-druzil94","name":"Druzil94","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T21:44:46-07:00","id":450123,"title":"","content":"If you have players who aren't interested in an introspective game about literal character development where the end goal is a happy, meaningful life where people leave you alone and you can make friends, and would rather indulge in smashing things around, you should probably not run Promethean for them. That's okay, every game isn't for everyone. And it's not a judgment on them, smashing is fun and can be conducive to more thoughtful and involved plots. (Smashing isn't even mutually exclusive with Promethean's premise and goals, but it sounds like your players reject the premise rather than just wanting to add smashing on top of it.)<br /> <br /> If the problem is your players don't see why a Promethean would want that end goal in general, well, not all of them do. There are the Hundred-Handed. But for the most part, being a near-indestructible titan of murderous terror isn't actually going to help you accomplish much in the way of goals as long as Disquiet and the Wasteland set you apart from the people around you. So you can smash things and are hard to kill; you can steal anything you want with impunity and wreck anybody who gets in your way. Okay. Now what? What are you gonna do with that, live alone in a cave on a bed of gold? If you stay there too long even the cave's gonna collapse on you out of spite.<br /> <br /> If your goal is to depopulate a town, I mean, yeah, you could probably stand good odds of accomplishing that before somebody thinks to burn it all down with fire and take you with them. Doesn't sound like it'd stay satisfying for long.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T22:01:55-07:00","id":450134,"title":"","content":"hmm because in my opinion ptc is an incredibly beautiful game concept but it requires a great deal of investment that not a lot of people are willing to put in","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5414-druzil94","name":"Druzil94","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T00:50:05-07:00","id":450225,"title":"","content":"All games require a certain investment and willingness of the players. I.e. Vampire needs everyone to be on board with the 'blood-drinking predator of the night' premise (ooc that is, ic your character can rail against it). And yeah, if that commitment is lacking you have to consider that maybe this is not the right game for this group.<br /> <br /> Promethean is a bit of an odd one out in this case, because the 'seeking to be human' premise is fairly unique. What you could try, is ask your players to just get with it for a short intro campaign (maybe four weekly sessions, or two monthly ones). That way they can see if it clicks for them. If it does (and it might, because the Pilgrimage offers great immersive roleplay imo) you can extend the intro into a full campaign. If it doesn't, then at least everyone gave it a shot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T02:34:33-07:00","id":450259,"title":"","content":"I'd highlight how each milestone towards the New Dawn truly makes the characters (and if you're really good the players themselves) feel like they've become a little more like a part of the world. Make the powers that the Prometheans use take a tole out of the characters in how they have to adapt and modify their bodies to chanel the powers and how the world rebels and rejects their unatural state through Disquiet, Wasteland, and of course (my new favorite) the Firestorms. When players begin to stray from the path bring in the grotesquery and body horror that's unique to Promethan's themselves to unnerve the players, and all the while have the storms build until the unnatural gathering of Pyros sparks a disaster that might bring ruin to what the Prometheans have worked towards or hold dear.<br /> <br /> Opp, and almost forgot to mention the Pandorans. Pandorans only wake up in the presence of Pyros so never let the players forget that wherever they go they're in danger of waking up monsters who want to eat them.<br /> <br /> That's how you show them how rewarding and sweet the New Dawn is to a Promethean. I personally suggest the Firestorm Chronicle Fiction Anthology for inspiration because that really helped me get my head around some of the more tricky concepts for running Promethean. And good luck. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Forgot to mention Pandorans. 03-20-2015, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:06:56-07:00","id":450674,"title":"","content":"I'd give a look at 2nd edition when it comes out. I feel like it incentivizes a lot of the Pilgrimage stuff better than the previous edition. More carrots /and/ sticks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T13:06:17-07:00","id":450777,"title":"","content":"I think the key takeaway is to demonstrate that all the tremendous power and strength granted by the Pyros can't make their real problems go away. Disquietism can stave off the pitchforks and torches for a night, and Vitality lets them tear apart the earth, but in the end, they're never going be accepted, and they'll never be comfortable in their own skins. Worse, their power makes them a target. Vampires and werewolves are going to take offense, mages are going to take an interest, and hunters are going to take up arms. The Promethean have a path laid out for them, but the ST has to make sure they see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T02:41:56-07:00","id":492469,"title":"","content":"Torments happen, which make a Promethean distrusted even amongst their fellows and they attract Pandorans too. They get derangements over feeling most negative situations they find themselves in and they can't even stay in one place for long lest it turns into a Wasteland. That's not even getting into times when they may need to do something that exposes their Disfigurements to mortals.<br /> True, I think we could do with more carrots for the Pilgrimage (the Athanor is a good one though), but there are loads of reasons why being a Promethean sucks and gaining a soul will make life more bearable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}